<section>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Command staff</div>
      <h2>The people behind the models</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="person">
      <div class="person-photo"><img
          src="/images/Manoj.png"
          alt="Manoj Tadepalli"><span class="id-tag">Co-Founder &amp; CEO</span></div>
      <div>
        <h3>Manoj Tadepalli</h3>
        <span class="role">Co-Founder &amp; Chief Executive Officer</span>
        <p>Marketing and retail domain lead of RainMan. Manoj has led the effort to make RainMan's services more
          oriented to marketing — promotions and pricing analytics as well as deep dives for distribution — and
          conceptualised the marketing data mart and scenario planner that lets companies move quickly into a high
          level of marketing analytics deployment while scaling company-wide.</p>
        <p>With 25 years' experience starting as an Account Manager and Planner at Ogilvy and FCB ULKA, Manoj has a
          deep grounding in branding, product management, distribution and innovation management. As head of marketing
          at Titan Industries, he spearheaded the turnaround of the Titan brand and the relaunch of Fastrack and
          Xylys. As a business head in international markets, he planned Titan's forays into South East Asia and the
          US, where his team that launched Tanishq won the Tata Group's Innovity award. He was also Country Manager at
          Enterprise IG for India.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="person">
      <div class="person-photo"><img
          src="/images/Balu.png"
          alt="V Balasubramanium"><span class="id-tag">Co-Founder &amp; MD</span></div>
      <div>
        <h3>V Balasubramanium</h3>
        <span class="role">Co-Founder &amp; Managing Director</span>
        <p>Media domain lead of RainMan, engaging with key clients on media investment management projects, and
          conceptualiser of RainMan's analytic benchmark tool, RainGauge. Balu spent 15+ years with WPP agencies —
          JWT, Ogilvy and GroupM — across India, China and global media planning, consumer insights and analytics.</p>
        <p>As Global CEO of Meritus Analytics (now Gain Theory), Balu led the growth of a top global analytics
          consultancy. He was earlier Director, Advanced Techniques Group and Insights for GroupM South Asia, where he
          conceived and set up the Global Analytic Centre. Balu is the winner of the WPP Global Atticus Grand Prix
          (1999) for his strategy paper "Measuring Passion."</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="person">
      <div class="person-photo"><img
          src="/images/KK.png" style="transform: scale(1.35) translateY(8%);"
          alt="Krishna Kumar CS"><span class="id-tag">Chief Analytics Officer</span></div>
      <div>
        <h3>Krishna Kumar CS</h3>
        <span class="role">Chief Analytics Officer &amp; Director</span>
        <p>Heads the analytics practice at RainMan, bringing innovation in technique and deploying the latest methods
          for actionable insight. KK's first brush with data-heavy projects began in the early 1990s at Ogilvy Direct,
          where he set up its first analytics team — later taking his expertise to Covansys (now CSC) and Reliance
          ADAG.</p>
        <p>A master of Marketing Mix Modelling with an in-depth knowledge of statistics, IT and marketing, KK has
          introduced many new methodologies to the field and is a visiting faculty in Analytics at the Narsee Monjee
          Institute of Management Studies (Bangalore campus).</p>
      </div>
    </div>

